8. Responsibilities of the Commission and the Councils (which should be known to the Students)
a) Any distress message received at the Anti -Ragging Helpline shall be simultaneously relayed to
the Vice Chancellor, the Warden of the Hostels, and if so required, th e District Magistrate, and
the Superintendent of Police, and shall also be web enabled so as to be in the public domain
simultaneously for the media and citizens to access it.
b) The Vice Chancellor shall be obliged to act immediately in response to the infor mation
received from the Anti -Ragging Helpline.
c) In order to enable a student or any person to communicate with the Anti -Ragging Helpline,
University shall permit unrestricted access to mobile phones and public phones in hostels and
campuses, other than in class -rooms, seminar halls, library, and in such other places that the
University may deem it necessary to restrict the use of phones.
